.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH ckman-piv-keys-generate 1  ckman 
.SH NAME
ckman\-piv\-keys\-generate \- Generate an asymmetric key pair on the device
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBckman\-piv\-keys\-generate\fR [\fB\-a\fR|\fB\-\-algorithm\fR] [\fB\-\-pin\-policy\fR] [\fB\-\-touch\-policy\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-m\fR|\fB\-\-management\-key\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISLOT\fR> <\fIPUBLIC_KEY_OUTPUT\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Generate an asymmetric key pair on the device
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-a\fR, \fB\-\-algorithm\fR \fI<ALGORITHM>\fR [default: rsa2048]
Algorithm to use in key generation
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
rsa1024
.IP \(bu 2
rsa2048
.IP \(bu 2
rsa3072
.IP \(bu 2
rsa4096
.IP \(bu 2
ecc\-p256
.IP \(bu 2
ecc\-p384
.IP \(bu 2
ecc\-p521
.IP \(bu 2
secp256k1
.IP \(bu 2
sm2
.IP \(bu 2
ed25519
.IP \(bu 2
x25519
.IP \(bu 2
ml\-dsa65
.IP \(bu 2
ml\-kem768
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-pin\-policy\fR \fI<PIN_POLICY>\fR
PIN policy for the key
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
never
.IP \(bu 2
once
.IP \(bu 2
always
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-touch\-policy\fR \fI<TOUCH_POLICY>\fR
Touch policy for the key
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
never
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
cached
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR [default: pem]
Output format
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
pem
.IP \(bu 2
der
.RE
.TP
\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-management\-key\fR \fI<MANAGEMENT_KEY>\fR
Current management key as 48 hex characters (prompted when needed)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fISLOT\fR>
PIV slot (9a, 9c, 9d, 9e, or retired 82\-95)
.TP
<\fIPUBLIC_KEY_OUTPUT\fR>
File to write the public key to (\*(Aq\-\*(Aq for stdout)
